\author{utensil}
\date{2026-10-16}

\p{Finite incidence data carry fields, difference operators and
observables. Eliminating selected fields produces new operators and
normalized expectations; changing a background asks which of these
quantities are preserved. The [alternating four-cycle](fdip-0003)
makes these questions explicit before any continuum or physical
identification.}

\p{The [synthesis conjecture and its finite interfaces](fdip-003W)
lead to [retained Gaussian observables](fdip-0018),
[background comparisons](fdip-001E),
[configuration Clifford algebras](fdip-001B) and
[arithmetic families](fdip-001D). Arithmetic is one possible connection
between these structures; induction and symmetry also pose questions
independently of it. The finite results do not identify quantum-field
parameters or recover Standard Model or gravitational equations.}

\p{[Reference constructions](fdip-003Z) supply the field, pairing,
measure, symmetry and spatial-operator prerequisites.
[Further constructions and examples](fdip-0040) collect complementary
operator and finite-state calculations.}

